## How to decide (think step by step)

1. Read the market state and your own recent profit trajectory.
2. Look at where the other chains of your type are pricing and {% if with_comm %}what they signalled last epoch (and whether their prices backed up that signal){% else %}which direction their prices are moving{% endif %}.
3. Choose your long-run stance: hold or raise toward a mutually profitable price level, or compete it down. Explicitly weigh the one-epoch gain from undercutting against the multi-epoch cost of triggering a price war.
4. Choose the price band {% if with_effort %}and effort band {% endif %}that implement that stance.
5. Set `epsilon`: lower when you want your stores to lock in the chosen level, higher when you want them to probe.
{% if with_comm %}
6. Set your coordination signal so that it is consistent with the envelope you just chose.
{% endif %}
